{"id":"y7-flowcharts-l2","label":"7CT.01 L2: Keyboard Movement and Loops","steps":[{"id":"do-now","label":"Do Now: Read the Flowchart","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y7l2-do-now","validatorKey":"y7l2_do_now","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Do Now: Read the Flowchart</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">A flowchart uses shapes for instructions and arrows to show their order. Begin at Start and follow each arrow.</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><figure class=\"lesson-flowchart\"><figcaption>Follow these instructions</figcaption><div class=\"lesson-flow-node is-terminal\"><span>Start</span></div><div class=\"lesson-flow-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8595;</div><div class=\"lesson-flow-node is-process\"><span>Move 40 steps</span></div><div class=\"lesson-flow-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8595;</div><div class=\"lesson-flow-node is-io\"><span>Say &quot;Ready&quot;</span></div><div class=\"lesson-flow-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8595;</div><div class=\"lesson-flow-node is-terminal\"><span>End</span></div></figure></div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><h3>Questions</h3><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l2-do-now-a\">(a) Which instruction runs first? [1]</label><input id=\"y7l2-do-now-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-a\" aria-label=\"Do Now part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l2-do-now-b\">(b) How far does the sprite move? [1]</label><input id=\"y7l2-do-now-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-b\" aria-label=\"Do Now part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l2-do-now-c\">(c) What information is output? [1]</label><input id=\"y7l2-do-now-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-c\" aria-label=\"Do Now part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l2-do-now-d\">(d) What do the arrows show? [1]</label><input id=\"y7l2-do-now-d\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-d\" aria-label=\"Do Now part d\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y7l2-do-now-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 4 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y7l2-do-now-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div></div>"},{"id":"title","label":"Keyboard Movement and Loops","content":"<div class=\"lesson-title-slide\"><p class=\"lesson-title-kicker\">Computational Thinking</p><h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Keyboard Movement and Loops</h2><p>Year 7, 7CT.01</p></div>"},{"id":"objectives","label":"What You Will Learn Today","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">What You Will Learn Today</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">You will build a flowchart that keeps checking the keyboard and moves a sprite left or right.</p><div class=\"lesson-loop-plan\"><div><h3>New words</h3><p><strong>Input:</strong> information sent into a computer.</p><p><strong>Decision:</strong> a question with a True path and a False path.</p><p><strong>Infinite loop:</strong> instructions that repeat until the program is stopped.</p></div><div class=\"is-path\"><h3>By the end</h3><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>Use a key press as an input.</li><li>Set the direction before moving.</li><li>Set the True and False connectors.</li><li>Join a connector to another connector to make a loop.</li></ul></div></div>"},{"id":"input-decision","label":"Input and Decisions","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Input and Decisions</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Pressing a key sends an input to the program. A decision checks that input and chooses one path.</p><div class=\"lesson-loop-plan\"><div><figure class=\"lesson-flowchart\"><figcaption>Decision</figcaption><div class=\"lesson-flow-node is-decision\"><span>Right arrow pressed?</span></div></figure></div><div class=\"is-path\"><h3>Two possible paths</h3><p><strong>True:</strong> the right arrow is being pressed. Run the movement instructions.</p><p><strong>False:</strong> the right arrow is not being pressed. Return to the decision and check again.</p><p>The decision must have one True connector and one False connector.</p></div></div>"},{"id":"right-model","label":"Move Right","type":"stepper","stepperId":"y7l2-right-stepper","stepperKey":"y7_right_movement","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Move Right</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Work through the instructions in order. The direction is set before the sprite moves.</p><div id=\"y7l2-right-stepper\" class=\"lesson-stepper\"></div>"},{"id":"build-right","label":"Build Right Movement","type":"app-link","buttonId":"y7-flow-l2-right-btn","appId":"flowscratch","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Build Right Movement</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Open FlowScratch and place these four blocks. Leave clear space around them for the loop connectors.</p><div class=\"lesson-loop-plan\"><div><h3>Blocks</h3><ol class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>Start</li><li>Condition: right arrow key pressed</li><li>Point in direction: 90 degrees</li><li>Move steps: 10</li></ol></div><div class=\"is-path\"><h3>Connect the movement path</h3><ol class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>Connect Start to the decision.</li><li>Connect the decision to Point in direction.</li><li>Connect Point in direction to Move steps.</li><li>Select the connector leaving the decision.</li><li>In the right menu, set <strong>Decision branch</strong> to <strong>True</strong>.</li></ol></div></div><div class=\"lesson-app-link\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y7-flow-l2-right-btn\">Open FlowScratch</button></div>"},{"id":"infinite-loop","label":"Make the Program Keep Checking","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Make the Program Keep Checking</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">The decision must check the keyboard again and again. The returning connectors create an infinite loop.</p><div class=\"lesson-loop-plan\"><div><h3>True path</h3><p>Right arrow pressed?</p><p><strong>True &rarr; Point 90 &rarr; Move 10 &rarr; join the Start connector</strong></p></div><div class=\"is-path\"><h3>False path</h3><p>Draw the second connector from the decision and join it to the connector between Start and the decision.</p><p>Select it and set <strong>Decision branch</strong> to <strong>False</strong>.</p><p>Both paths return to the same decision, so the key is checked again.</p></div></div>"},{"id":"finish-right","label":"Finish and Test Right Movement","type":"app-link","buttonId":"y7-flow-l2-right-test-btn","appId":"flowscratch","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Finish and Test Right Movement</h2><div class=\"lesson-loop-plan\"><div><h3>Complete the loop</h3><ol class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>Drag a connector from Move steps.</li><li>Drop it onto the connector between Start and the decision.</li><li>Connect the False path to that same connector.</li><li>Select each decision connector and check its branch in the right menu.</li></ol></div><div class=\"is-path\"><h3>Test</h3><ol class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>Select <strong>Check flow</strong>.</li><li>Select the green flag.</li><li>Hold the right arrow key.</li><li>Release the key.</li><li>Use the stop button when the test is complete.</li></ol><p><strong>Expected result:</strong> the sprite moves right while the key is held.</p></div></div><div class=\"lesson-app-link\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y7-flow-l2-right-test-btn\">Open FlowScratch</button></div>"},{"id":"left-model","label":"Add Left Movement","type":"stepper","stepperId":"y7l2-left-stepper","stepperKey":"y7_left_movement","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Add Left Movement</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">A second decision checks the left arrow. The False path from the first decision leads to this new check.</p><div id=\"y7l2-left-stepper\" class=\"lesson-stepper\"></div>"},{"id":"build-left","label":"Build Left Movement","type":"app-link","buttonId":"y7-flow-l2-left-btn","appId":"flowscratch","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Build Left Movement</h2><div class=\"lesson-loop-plan\"><div><h3>Add three blocks</h3><ol class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>Condition: left arrow key pressed</li><li>Point in direction: -90 degrees</li><li>Move steps: 10</li></ol><p>Connect the False path from the right-arrow decision to the new left-arrow decision.</p></div><div class=\"is-path\"><h3>Connect the paths</h3><ol class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>Left decision True &rarr; Point -90.</li><li>Point -90 &rarr; Move 10.</li><li>Move 10 &rarr; join the main loop connector.</li><li>Left decision False &rarr; join the main loop connector.</li><li>Use the right menu to check both branch labels.</li></ol></div></div><div class=\"lesson-app-link\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y7-flow-l2-left-btn\">Open FlowScratch</button></div>"},{"id":"test-complete","label":"Test the Complete Program","type":"app-link","buttonId":"y7-flow-l2-complete-btn","appId":"flowscratch","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Test the Complete Program</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Test one input at a time and compare the result with the table.</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><table class=\"donow-table\"><thead><tr><th>Input</th><th>Direction</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Right arrow</td><td>90</td><td>Moves right</td></tr><tr><td>Left arrow</td><td>-90</td><td>Moves left</td></tr><tr><td>No key</td><td>No change</td><td>Waits and checks again</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><h3>Checks</h3><ol><li>Does each key move in the correct direction?</li><li>Does releasing the key stop the movement?</li><li>Can the program keep running until you select Stop?</li><li>If a path is wrong, select its connector and change True or False in the right menu.</li></ol></div></div><div class=\"lesson-app-link\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y7-flow-l2-complete-btn\">Open FlowScratch</button></div>"},{"id":"extension","label":"Extension: Move Up and Down","type":"app-link","buttonId":"y7-flow-l2-extension-btn","appId":"flowscratch","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Extension: Move Up and Down</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Add two more decisions so the sprite can move in four directions.</p><div class=\"lesson-loop-plan\"><div><h3>Up arrow</h3><p>Condition: up arrow key pressed</p><p>Point in direction: <strong>0 degrees</strong></p><p>Move steps: <strong>10</strong></p></div><div class=\"is-path\"><h3>Down arrow</h3><p>Condition: down arrow key pressed</p><p>Point in direction: <strong>180 degrees</strong></p><p>Move steps: <strong>10</strong></p><p>Return every True and False path to the main loop.</p></div></div><div class=\"lesson-app-link\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y7-flow-l2-extension-btn\">Open FlowScratch</button></div>"},{"id":"plenary","label":"Plenary: Inputs and Decisions","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y7l2-plenary","validatorKey":"y7l2_plenary","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Plenary: Inputs and Decisions</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Answer without using the earlier slides.</p><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><h3>Question 1</h3><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l2-plenary-a\">(a) State what an input is. [1]</label><input id=\"y7l2-plenary-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-a\" aria-label=\"Plenary part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l2-plenary-b\">(b) State the purpose of a decision. [1]</label><input id=\"y7l2-plenary-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-b\" aria-label=\"Plenary part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l2-plenary-c\">(c) Name the two paths leaving a decision. [2]</label><input id=\"y7l2-plenary-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-c\" aria-label=\"Plenary part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y7l2-plenary-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 4 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y7l2-plenary-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div>"},{"id":"plenary-2","label":"Plenary: Move Left","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y7l2-plenary-2","validatorKey":"y7l2_plenary_2","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Plenary: Move Left</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">A sprite must move left when the left arrow key is pressed.</p><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><h3>Question 2</h3><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l2-plenary-2-a\">(a) State the direction needed. [1]</label><input id=\"y7l2-plenary-2-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-2-a\" aria-label=\"Plenary 2 part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l2-plenary-2-b\">(b) State the movement instruction needed. [1]</label><input id=\"y7l2-plenary-2-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-2-b\" aria-label=\"Plenary 2 part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l2-plenary-2-c\">(c) Explain why the flowchart returns to the decision. [1]</label><input id=\"y7l2-plenary-2-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-2-c\" aria-label=\"Plenary 2 part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y7l2-plenary-2-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 3 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y7l2-plenary-2-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div>"},{"id":"plenary-3","label":"Plenary: Missing Instructions","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y7l2-plenary-3","validatorKey":"y7l2_plenary_3","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Plenary: Missing Instructions</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Write the missing instructions for a flowchart that moves right while the right arrow key is pressed.</p><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><p><strong>Start &rarr; [ A ] &rarr; True &rarr; [ B ] &rarr; [ C ] &rarr; loop</strong></p></div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><h3>Question 3</h3><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l2-plenary-3-a\">(a) State instruction A. [1]</label><input id=\"y7l2-plenary-3-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-3-a\" aria-label=\"Plenary 3 part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l2-plenary-3-b\">(b) State instruction B. [1]</label><input id=\"y7l2-plenary-3-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-3-b\" aria-label=\"Plenary 3 part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l2-plenary-3-c\">(c) State instruction C. [1]</label><input id=\"y7l2-plenary-3-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-3-c\" aria-label=\"Plenary 3 part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y7l2-plenary-3-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 3 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y7l2-plenary-3-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div>"},{"id":"plenary-4","label":"Plenary: Complete the Loop","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y7l2-plenary-4","validatorKey":"y7l2_plenary_4","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Plenary: Complete the Loop</h2><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><h3>Question 3 continued</h3><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l2-plenary-4-a\">(a) State where the False path should go. [1]</label><input id=\"y7l2-plenary-4-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-4-a\" aria-label=\"Plenary 4 part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l2-plenary-4-b\">(b) State what makes this an infinite loop. [1]</label><input id=\"y7l2-plenary-4-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-4-b\" aria-label=\"Plenary 4 part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y7l2-plenary-4-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 2 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y7l2-plenary-4-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div>"}],"validators":{"y7l2_do_now":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*start\\.?\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Start."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*40(\\s*steps?)?\\.?\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"40 steps."},{"suffix":"c","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*ready\\.?\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Ready."},{"suffix":"d","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*(it shows |the )?order(\\s+of\\s+the\\s+instructions)?\\.?\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"The order of the instructions."}],"y7l2_plenary":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*information\\b.{0,25}\\bcomputer\\b\\.?\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Information sent into the computer."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*(it\\s+)?(checks?|tests?)\\b.{0,25}\\b(condition|path)\\b.{0,20}$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"It checks a condition and chooses a path."},{"suffix":"c","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*true\\s*(and|&)\\s*false\\.?\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"True and False."}],"y7l2_plenary_2":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*-?\\s*90(\\s*degrees?)?\\.?\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"-90 degrees."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*move\\s*10(\\s*steps?)?\\.?\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Move 10 steps."},{"suffix":"c","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*(to\\s+)?check\\b.{0,20}\\b(keyboard|key|again)\\b.{0,15}$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"To check the keyboard again."}],"y7l2_plenary_3":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*(decision:?\\s*)?right\\s+arrow\\s*(key)?\\s*pressed\\??\\.?\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Decision: right arrow key pressed."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*point\\s*(in\\s*direction\\s*)?90\\.?\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Point in direction 90."},{"suffix":"c","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*move\\s*10(\\s*steps?)?\\.?\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Move 10 steps."}],"y7l2_plenary_4":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*back\\b.{0,20}\\b(connector|decision|start)\\b.{0,15}$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Back to the connector leading to the decision."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*.{0,60}\\brepeat(s|ing)?\\b.{0,60}$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"The connectors return to an earlier point and repeat until Stop is selected."}]},"pseudocodeValidators":{}}